WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.040
One of Thor's funniest friends will return
for the Asgardian hero's next cinematic venture.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.000
During a recent interview, director Taika
Waititi, who helmed the franchise-reviver

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.900
Thor: Ragnarok and will also direct Thor:
Love and Thunder, confirmed the return of

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.460
a fan-favorite character.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.700
His name, of course, is Korg, and he's coming
back to the big screen for more Thor.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:23.460
Though his conversation with Jimmy Kimmel
was mostly about his buzzy new film Jojo Rabbit,

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.019
Waititi briefly touched on Thor: Love and
Thunder, which is when the director made this

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.340
exciting announcement.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.200
"My character's coming back.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.240
Korg."

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.980
A member of an ancient group of rock-like
humanoid entities, Korg made his official

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.660
debut in Thor: Ragnarok, but he actually wasn't
the first Kronan to appear in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:45.440
Universe.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.020
The MCU canon details that a prominent member
of the Marauders, the coalition of invaders

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:54.720
that attacked the Nine Realms including Thor's
home world of Asgard, was a Kronan warrior.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.320
That Kronan tried to throw down with Thor
during the battle on Vanaheim in 2013's Thor:

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.930
The Dark World, but the God of Thunder took
him down.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:07.040
In 2017's Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2,
two Kronans were shown fighting when the Quadrant

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.060
whizzed past them.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:12.000
Many fans have speculated that one of the
two Kronans was Korg, who wound up getting

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.560
sent to Sakaar and was forced to compete in
the Grandmaster's Contest of Champions.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.400
In Thor: Ragnarok, Korg meets Thor in a holding
area where the Grandmaster's champions prepare

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.080
to fight.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.560
"I tried to start a revolution, but I didn't
print enough pamphlets, so hardly anyone showed

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.180
up except my mum and her boyfriend, who I
hate."

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.080
The two quickly become allies and Korg ultimately
stages a mutiny against the Grandmaster.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.220
Korg escapes from Sakaar and pops up again
to help defeat the villainous Hela on the

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.390
Rainbow Bridge leading into Asgard.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:45.350
After the fiery demon Surtur rises again and
destroys Asgard at the end of Thor: Ragnarok,

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.460
Korg sticks around with his godly buddy.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:52.120
Though he didn't appear in Avengers: Infinity
War, Korg emerged as a lucky survivor of Thanos'

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.720
Snap in Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:58.000
With half the universe's population gone,
Korg and Miek reunited with Thor and lived

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.280
together in New Asgard.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.040
For five years, Korg provided emotional support
as Thor struggled with his feelings, and Korg

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.720
even lent a hand in the final fight against
Thanos.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.220
All this is to say that Korg has been an important
part of Thor's life for many years, and that's

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:15.019
not going to change in Thor: Love and Thunder,
which will likely start off by filling us

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.820
in on what's happened since we last saw Korg
and Thor.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.139
Embracing his bigger body and knowing that
he's still worthy of being a hero, Thor joined

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:26.370
forces with the Guardians of the Galaxy in
the final moments of Endgame, when the galaxy-saving

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.800
crew were about to ship out in search of Gamora.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.840
Meanwhile, Korg headed home to New Asgard,
where Valkyrie is now king.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:36.920
While we can't speculate on what might happen
in the upcoming third Guardians of the Galaxy

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:41.400
movie which might see Thor in the mix, we
can theorize that Thor: Love and Thunder will

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.940
see Thor returning home to New Asgard and
having a happy reunion with Korg and Valkyrie.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.739
Waititi has confirmed that Love and Thunder
will introduce the MCU's first openly bisexual

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:54.040
character in Valkyrie, who will be looking
for her queen in the new movie.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.920
It seems safe to assume that Love and Thunder
might see Korg serving as one of Valkyrie's

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.100
royal advisors, helping her find a lucky lady
to aid in ruling New Asgard.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.200
Whichever way the cookie crumbles, Korg is
sure to bring plenty of laughs and some rocky

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.340
shoulders to cry on should anyone need them
in the new Thor flick.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:13.319
The only bad news about Thor: Love and Thunder
thus far, however, is that fans will have

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.320
to wait until November 5, 2021 to see it.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.640
Until then, there's undoubtedly plenty of
exciting news to come for the God of Thunder.

